## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses practical data ingestion resilience, including handling mixed encodings and multi-channel sources (SFTP for CSVs, REST for JSON), along with end-to-end lineage and data quality understanding.

## Key Concepts
- Encoding detection and transcoding at ingestion
- Incremental loading using per-file watermarks
- Mapping Data Flows for Parquet conversion and star schema population in Azure Synapse
- Data quality and schema validation checks
- Purview lineage integration for traceability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function to detect encoding and transcode to UTF-8
const fs = require('fs');
module.exports = async function (context, myBlob) {
    const buffer = Buffer.from(myBlob);
    const isUtf16 = buffer[0] === 0xFF && buffer[1] === 0xFE;
    let content;

    if (isUtf16) {
        content = buffer.toString('utf16le');
    } else {
        content = buffer.toString('utf8');
    }

    context.bindings.outputBlob = content;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design decisions for a unified real-time and batch ingestion platform, data governance, schema management, late data handling, and cross-service upserts in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Delta Live Tables, Delta Lake, Purview lineage, MERGE upserts
- Event-time processing, watermarks, late data handling
- Ingest from Azure Event Hubs and on-prem SFTP into ADLS Gen2
- Synapse Analytics star schema load and Delta Lake schema evolution
- Artifact layout, lineage tagging, cost-aware orchestration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-schema validation for streaming records
function validate(record, schema) {
  const required = schema.required || [];
  const missing = required.filter(k => !(k in record));
  if (missing.length) throw new Error("Missing fields: " + missing.join(", "));
  if (schema.types) {
    for (const [k, t] of Object.entries(schema.types)) {
      if (typeof record[k] !== t) throw new Error("Invalid type for " + k);
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

